1
00:00:00,867 --> 00:00:05,305
The Iranians are more aware than ever
that they're in the driver's seat.

2
00:00:05,338 --> 00:00:09,976
They're are more aware than ever
that President Trump is in deep trouble

3
00:00:10,443 --> 00:00:13,513
and that he needs an agreement.

4
00:00:13,813 --> 00:00:18,151
The West is leading
Ukraine down the primrose path

5
00:00:18,151 --> 00:00:22,288
The Israelis
are executing a genocide in Gaza.

6
00:00:22,355 --> 00:00:26,026
It's not China's fault
that it wants to be powerful.

7
00:00:26,059 --> 00:00:28,000
So if you get into trouble

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,899
and you dial 911, there's nobody at the other end

9
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:38,271
Hi, this is John Mearsheimer,
and I'm back again with another episode.

10
00:00:38,505 --> 00:00:42,042
And this time
I want to talk about the Iran war.

11
00:00:42,142 --> 00:00:45,145
And what I'd like to argue here

12
00:00:45,145 --> 00:00:50,383
is that it's time for President Trump
to settle this war,

13
00:00:50,417 --> 00:00:55,188
to reach an agreement
with the Iranians, to put an end to it

14
00:00:55,188 --> 00:01:01,194
and, in effect, to accept defeat,
to recognize that you

15
00:01:01,227 --> 00:01:06,299
that that Iran has won this war 
and that we have lost the war.

16
00:01:06,299 --> 00:01:12,238
And the way I'd like to proceed
is I'd first like to talk about the goals

17
00:01:12,472 --> 00:01:18,278
that the United States set out to achieve
at the start of this war.

18
00:01:18,411 --> 00:01:25,251
And then I'd like to talk about
our failure to achieve any of those goals.

19
00:01:25,251 --> 00:01:29,255
And I like to describe how badly off
we are

20
00:01:29,322 --> 00:01:34,060
in terms of having pursued
these particular goals.

21
00:01:34,094 --> 00:01:38,898
And then I want to switch
and talk about the military strategies

22
00:01:38,898 --> 00:01:43,303
that we have employed
in pursuit of those goals.

23
00:01:43,303 --> 00:01:45,972
And of course, the argument
that I'm going to make

24
00:01:45,972 --> 00:01:49,676
is that the different strategies
that we have employed

25
00:01:49,709 --> 00:01:53,713
have failed to achieve

26
00:01:53,713 --> 00:01:57,851
the goals
that we set out with in this war.

27
00:01:57,851 --> 00:02:00,053
And I want to talk at some length

28
00:02:00,053 --> 00:02:04,457
about those different strategies
and why they failed.

29
00:02:04,457 --> 00:02:08,695
And I'm going to make the argument,
as will become clear, that there were five

30
00:02:08,695 --> 00:02:13,266
potential strategies
that the United States could pursue.

31
00:02:13,299 --> 00:02:18,538
It only pursued three of them to
it did not pursue.

32
00:02:18,538 --> 00:02:22,709
And I'll talk about those three strategies
and why they failed.

33
00:02:22,709 --> 00:02:26,813
And then I'll talk
about the two strategies we didn't pursue

34
00:02:26,813 --> 00:02:29,816
and why we did not pursue them.

35
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:34,854
And you want to keep in mind here
that what I'm going to be constantly

36
00:02:34,854 --> 00:02:39,592
doing is talking about the relationship
between the goals that we're pursuing

37
00:02:39,592 --> 00:02:45,331
and the strategies that we adopted
or didn't adopt to achieve those goals.

38
00:02:45,331 --> 00:02:47,500
But let's start with the goals.

39
00:02:48,902 --> 00:02:51,771
When the war started, the United States,

40
00:02:51,771 --> 00:02:55,642
and this was true of the Israelis as well,
had four goals.

41
00:02:56,242 --> 00:03:00,079
The first goal was regime
change in Tehran.

42
00:03:00,513 --> 00:03:06,386
The second goal was to make sure
to eliminate

43
00:03:06,719 --> 00:03:12,025
Iran's ability to enrich uranium,
because if you can enrich uranium,

44
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:15,828
you can rather easily
make a nuclear weapon.

45
00:03:16,196 --> 00:03:19,199
The third goal was to eliminate

46
00:03:19,666 --> 00:03:21,834
Ukraine's long range ballistic

47
00:03:21,834 --> 00:03:24,837
missile program, and the fourth goal

48
00:03:24,837 --> 00:03:28,908
was to basically get Iran

49
00:03:28,908 --> 00:03:33,613
to no longer support Hamas, Hezbollah
and the Houthis.

50
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:35,114
Those were the four goals.

51
00:03:35,114 --> 00:03:39,118
And very importantly, I think
regime change was the most important

52
00:03:39,152 --> 00:03:42,956
of those four goals,
because if you didn't achieve regime

53
00:03:42,956 --> 00:03:46,960
change, you really could not achieve
the other three goals.

54
00:03:46,993 --> 00:03:50,930
So regime change was the numero uno goal.

55
00:03:50,997 --> 00:03:55,068
But you still had these three other
very important goals

56
00:03:55,068 --> 00:03:59,138
that were, in my opinion,
subordinated to that overarching goal.

57
00:03:59,339 --> 00:04:03,076
Now, the question
you want to ask yourself is

58
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:07,180
where are we today
in terms of those goals?

59
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:10,717
And let me make two different
sets of arguments here.

60
00:04:11,184 --> 00:04:14,187
First of all,
just looking at the four goals

61
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:20,193
we have achieved, none of the four goals,
none of them have been achieved,

62
00:04:20,193 --> 00:04:25,431
and there's no evidence any of them
are going to be achieved anytime soon.

63
00:04:25,465 --> 00:04:29,502
In addition to that,
we are now in a situation

64
00:04:29,502 --> 00:04:34,040
which we were not in back on February
27th, the day before the war

65
00:04:34,073 --> 00:04:37,176
started, where Iran controls

66
00:04:37,176 --> 00:04:41,381
the Strait of Hormuz
and today, as we speak,

67
00:04:41,414 --> 00:04:44,384
has shut off the flow of traffic

68
00:04:44,384 --> 00:04:47,387
in and out of the Strait of Hormuz.

69
00:04:47,453 --> 00:04:51,624
Furthermore, on February 27th,
the day before the war, the United States

70
00:04:51,624 --> 00:04:54,827
had a robust alliance structure

71
00:04:54,827 --> 00:04:58,264
with the Gulf states in the region,

72
00:04:58,264 --> 00:05:02,235
and it had serious set

73
00:05:02,268 --> 00:05:05,638
of military bases in the region.

74
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:09,509
Today, those bases have been either badly

75
00:05:09,509 --> 00:05:13,980
damaged or destroyed,
and the alliance structure

76
00:05:14,013 --> 00:05:19,185
that the United States had with the Gulf
states has been basically

77
00:05:19,752 --> 00:05:22,588
torn to tatters.

78
00:05:22,588 --> 00:05:24,424
To take this a step further.

79
00:05:24,424 --> 00:05:28,695
The international economy,
because of the blockade

80
00:05:28,961 --> 00:05:34,200
on the Strait of Hormuz,
is in a very dangerous situation,

81
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:38,504
and there is a real risk
of a worldwide depression

82
00:05:38,504 --> 00:05:42,108
if this war is not settled sometime soon.

83
00:05:42,108 --> 00:05:47,714
And then finally, I would note that China,
which is America's principal adversary,

84
00:05:47,714 --> 00:05:50,817
according to the Trump administration,

85
00:05:50,817 --> 00:05:54,320
has benefited
enormously from this conflict.

86
00:05:54,787 --> 00:05:59,826
So this is a situation
where the United States

87
00:05:59,826 --> 00:06:03,796
has not only not achieved
any of the four goals it set out with,

88
00:06:03,830 --> 00:06:07,667
it also has a number of other

89
00:06:07,734 --> 00:06:11,137
serious problems today that did not exist.

90
00:06:11,137 --> 00:06:14,173
On February 27th, the day before the war
started.

91
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:17,410
Let me come at this
from a different perspective.

92
00:06:17,777 --> 00:06:20,813
If you look at the memorandum
of understanding

93
00:06:21,381 --> 00:06:26,819
that President Trump
signed with the Iranians on June

94
00:06:26,819 --> 00:06:30,423
17th of this year, this member

95
00:06:30,790 --> 00:06:35,061
memorandum of understanding
was designed to shut the war down.

96
00:06:35,228 --> 00:06:39,899
What you see is that that was basically
a surrender document.

97
00:06:39,932 --> 00:06:45,104
President Trump
basically conceded every point

98
00:06:45,104 --> 00:06:50,109
that was at issue between the Iranians
and the Americans.

99
00:06:50,309 --> 00:06:54,547
The way the document was set up,
this is the memorandum of understanding,

100
00:06:54,547 --> 00:07:00,353
is that we would have a cease
fire up front.

101
00:07:00,586 --> 00:07:06,592
The the fighting would stop and
the Strait of Hormuz would be opened up.

102
00:07:06,893 --> 00:07:11,731
And furthermore,
the Iranians would be able to sell

103
00:07:11,731 --> 00:07:16,869
all on the open markets,
which had not been the case before.

104
00:07:17,336 --> 00:07:22,442
The June 17th
memorandum of understanding was signed.

105
00:07:22,475 --> 00:07:25,511
They could sell all without

106
00:07:25,511 --> 00:07:29,348
having to worry about American sanctions.

107
00:07:29,482 --> 00:07:33,453
That was the first part of the agreement,
again, to get a cease fire, number one

108
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:37,256
and number two to open up the strait.

109
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:41,093
Then there would be a 60 day
negotiating period.

110
00:07:41,093 --> 00:07:45,231
And at the end of that 60 day
negotiating period,

111
00:07:45,698 --> 00:07:49,135
there would be a decision
on the nuclear issue.

112
00:07:49,135 --> 00:07:53,573
But it was very clear that the Iranians

113
00:07:53,573 --> 00:07:56,742
would maintain
a nuclear enrichment capability,

114
00:07:56,776 --> 00:08:01,080
which was at odds with one of the goals
we had going into the war.

115
00:08:01,614 --> 00:08:07,253
Furthermore, it was clear that the
United States would have to

116
00:08:08,521 --> 00:08:11,190
allow all of those frozen

117
00:08:11,190 --> 00:08:15,495
Iranian assets to go back to Iran.

118
00:08:15,828 --> 00:08:18,898
And furthermore, reparations

119
00:08:18,898 --> 00:08:21,901
would have to be paid to.

120
00:08:23,736 --> 00:08:24,570
The Iranians

121
00:08:24,570 --> 00:08:29,375
for all of the damage
that was done to Iran in this war.

122
00:08:29,442 --> 00:08:31,878
And an enormous amount of damage was done.

123
00:08:31,878 --> 00:08:36,282
So an enormous amount of money
would have to be paid to the Iranians.

124
00:08:37,650 --> 00:08:41,921
And on top of all of this,

125
00:08:41,954 --> 00:08:48,961
the Iranians would be able to sell
all freely on world markets.

126
00:08:48,961 --> 00:08:54,333
So all of this is to say that if you look
at the memorandum of understanding,

127
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:58,437
the United States conceded on
every key issue,

128
00:08:58,971 --> 00:09:02,642
the Iranians prevailed.

129
00:09:03,075 --> 00:09:07,947
So in terms of the goals
that we went into this war with,

130
00:09:07,980 --> 00:09:11,951
we failed to achieve any of them,
and we ended up much worse,

131
00:09:12,318 --> 00:09:17,456
much worse off after the war got going.

132
00:09:17,590 --> 00:09:21,661
Now, the question you have to ask yourself
is what happened here?

133
00:09:22,295 --> 00:09:26,032
We had a set of different
military strategies

134
00:09:26,032 --> 00:09:29,735
that we tried to use

135
00:09:30,136 --> 00:09:34,507
to achieve those four goals
that we set out with.

136
00:09:34,540 --> 00:09:39,278
And the question you want to ask
yourself is what were those strategies

137
00:09:39,712 --> 00:09:42,381
and why did they fail?

138
00:09:42,381 --> 00:09:46,919
Now when I'd like to do
is I'd like to frame the discussion

139
00:09:46,953 --> 00:09:49,956
in terms of what I think are the five

140
00:09:49,989 --> 00:09:52,892
possible strategies that the United States

141
00:09:52,892 --> 00:09:58,698
was presented with,
and then describe what happened,

142
00:09:58,731 --> 00:10:03,235
and then analyze
why the strategies didn't fail.

143
00:10:03,402 --> 00:10:04,670
So I'm going to lay out

144
00:10:04,670 --> 00:10:08,741
the five strategies
that I'm going to describe what happened

145
00:10:08,975 --> 00:10:14,146
from February 28th up to the present
in terms of employing those strategies.

146
00:10:14,146 --> 00:10:17,216
And then I'm going to analyze
why they failed.

147
00:10:17,850 --> 00:10:19,652
Here are the five strategies.

148
00:10:19,652 --> 00:10:22,521
The first three involve air power.

149
00:10:22,521 --> 00:10:25,024
The fourth involves naval power

150
00:10:25,024 --> 00:10:28,494
and the fifth involves
land power or armies.

151
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:31,797
Regarding air power.

152
00:10:31,797 --> 00:10:34,800
The first strategy is what I would call

153
00:10:34,934 --> 00:10:37,870
discriminate

154
00:10:37,870 --> 00:10:39,739
air campaign.

155
00:10:39,739 --> 00:10:42,908
Okay, a discriminate air campaign.

156
00:10:43,376 --> 00:10:48,514
And when I say discriminate,
a discriminate air campaign is basically

157
00:10:48,514 --> 00:10:54,720
a strategic bombing campaign
where you do not go after certain targets.

158
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:56,255
In other words, you discriminate.

159
00:10:56,255 --> 00:11:01,427
And in this case,
a discriminate air campaign involves going

160
00:11:01,427 --> 00:11:05,097
after military targets,

161
00:11:05,464 --> 00:11:10,136
a handful of civilian targets
and civilian infrastructure,

162
00:11:10,136 --> 00:11:16,375
but basically staying away from
massive attacks on civilian infrastructure

163
00:11:16,375 --> 00:11:22,581
and staying away from the facilities
in Iran.

164
00:11:22,615 --> 00:11:26,752
Now, when I say civilian infrastructure,
this means staying away from bridges,

165
00:11:27,586 --> 00:11:30,222
staying away from attacking bridges,
staying away

166
00:11:30,222 --> 00:11:34,860
from attacking power stations,
and of course, staying away

167
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:38,064
from attacking the oil facilities,

168
00:11:38,064 --> 00:11:41,400
the oil and gas facilities inside of Iran.

169
00:11:41,434 --> 00:11:46,472
This is what a discriminate air campaign,

170
00:11:46,505 --> 00:11:51,077
a discriminate strategic bombing
campaign looks like.

171
00:11:51,744 --> 00:11:54,513
I contrast that

172
00:11:54,513 --> 00:11:57,817
with an indiscriminate air campaign.

173
00:11:57,983 --> 00:12:03,255
And indiscriminate
air campaign is where the United States

174
00:12:03,255 --> 00:12:07,660
and the Israelis go
after all of the targets

175
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:12,531
that I just described as being legitimate
in a discriminatory campaign,

176
00:12:12,531 --> 00:12:16,936
but also going after civilian
infrastructure, power stations,

177
00:12:16,936 --> 00:12:22,942
bridges and going after all facilities,
in other words, targeting

178
00:12:23,075 --> 00:12:26,312
all of the possible

179
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:29,949
targets inside of Iran.

180
00:12:29,982 --> 00:12:35,187
That's an indiscriminate air campaign
as opposed to a discriminate air campaign.

181
00:12:35,321 --> 00:12:41,494
The third strategy is tit for tat,
and this is an air campaign as well.

182
00:12:41,594 --> 00:12:46,899
But it involves small scale attacks
where one side

183
00:12:46,932 --> 00:12:50,569
hits the other
and then the other hits back.

184
00:12:50,703 --> 00:12:53,506
And that's what I call tit for tat.

185
00:12:53,506 --> 00:12:59,345
It's on a much smaller scale
than either the discriminant

186
00:12:59,345 --> 00:13:04,150
or indiscriminate strategic bombing
campaigns, much more limited.

187
00:13:04,183 --> 00:13:07,953
So those are the three strategies
that involve air power.

188
00:13:07,987 --> 00:13:11,423
Then the the one strategy that involves

189
00:13:11,423 --> 00:13:15,227
naval power is a blockade,
a maritime blockade.

190
00:13:15,227 --> 00:13:18,497
And in this case, the Iranians

191
00:13:19,865 --> 00:13:23,435
are blockaded by the US Navy.

192
00:13:23,636 --> 00:13:26,705
Then the final option involves the army.

193
00:13:26,705 --> 00:13:28,841
And this is a ground invasion.

194
00:13:28,841 --> 00:13:31,811
This is a land attack against Iran.

195
00:13:31,877 --> 00:13:35,014
The United States could try and conquer

196
00:13:35,014 --> 00:13:38,450
an island or two
that belong to Iran in the Persian Gulf.

197
00:13:38,450 --> 00:13:43,622
It could, in the United States
could try to invade the Iranian mainland.

198
00:13:43,622 --> 00:13:47,693
It could concentrate
on all of the territory that Iran controls

199
00:13:47,693 --> 00:13:51,397
around the Strait of Hormuz,
for the purpose of trying

200
00:13:51,430 --> 00:13:55,501
to open the Strait of Hormuz
with land power.

201
00:13:55,534 --> 00:13:59,438
So those are the five strategies

202
00:13:59,438 --> 00:14:04,677
that the United States had on its menu.

203
00:14:04,710 --> 00:14:08,314
Now, let me switch gears and describe

204
00:14:08,347 --> 00:14:12,952
which strategies the United States used
at which points in time.

205
00:14:13,052 --> 00:14:15,588
And then I want to analyze them.

206
00:14:15,588 --> 00:14:17,623
And of course, what I analyze them.

207
00:14:17,623 --> 00:14:20,626
What I'm going to try to do is

208
00:14:20,626 --> 00:14:24,597
explain why those strategies
failed to achieve the goals

209
00:14:24,597 --> 00:14:30,469
that the United States was pursuing
when it started the war on February 28th.

210
00:14:30,469 --> 00:14:35,641
But to go to the description
on February 28th, when the United States

211
00:14:35,674 --> 00:14:40,379
launches the air war,
which lasts until April

212
00:14:40,379 --> 00:14:43,849
8th, it's basically a 40 day war.

213
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:49,121
The United States pursues
a discriminate air campaign.

214
00:14:49,388 --> 00:14:53,959
They start off, as almost everybody
acknowledges, with a shock

215
00:14:53,959 --> 00:14:58,797
and awe campaign
that's designed to decapitate the regime.

216
00:14:58,831 --> 00:15:02,034
And in fact, the United States

217
00:15:02,034 --> 00:15:06,505
and the Israelis are successful
at decapitating the regime,

218
00:15:06,639 --> 00:15:10,743
and they clearly launch a shock
and awe strategy.

219
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:14,213
But it's all part of a discriminate air
campaign.

220
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:18,384
It's very important
to understand that, with a few exceptions,

221
00:15:18,550 --> 00:15:23,022
the United States
and the Israelis do not hit

222
00:15:24,056 --> 00:15:26,025
power plants,

223
00:15:26,025 --> 00:15:29,628
civilian bridges or,

224
00:15:30,796 --> 00:15:34,633
well, facilities and gas facilities
in Iran.

225
00:15:34,667 --> 00:15:38,737
In other words, it's
not an indiscriminate air campaign.

226
00:15:38,737 --> 00:15:40,472
It's a discriminated air campaign.

227
00:15:40,472 --> 00:15:43,475
And it lasts 40 days.

228
00:15:44,109 --> 00:15:47,079
At the end of those 40

229
00:15:47,079 --> 00:15:50,616
days, a cease fire is put in place.

230
00:15:50,749 --> 00:15:55,120
But it's very important to understand that
right before

231
00:15:56,255 --> 00:15:59,792
right before the cease fire on April 8th,

232
00:16:00,059 --> 00:16:03,395
President Trump was talking about

233
00:16:03,429 --> 00:16:07,199
putting Iran back in the Stone age.

234
00:16:07,232 --> 00:16:10,869
On April 7th, he said,
this is on April 7th.

235
00:16:11,036 --> 00:16:15,574
A whole civilization will die tonight.

236
00:16:16,909 --> 00:16:21,880
What's going on here is that President
Trump, over the course of the 40 day

237
00:16:21,914 --> 00:16:27,186
war, is beginning to think about moving
from a discriminate air

238
00:16:27,219 --> 00:16:31,991
campaign to an indiscriminate air campaign
that's on April 7th.

239
00:16:32,024 --> 00:16:36,161
He makes that comment
about a whole civilization

240
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:38,063
dying.

241
00:16:38,063 --> 00:16:40,032
Okay, that's on April 7th.

242
00:16:40,032 --> 00:16:44,336
Then on April 8th, he switches gears
and we've seen him do this many times.

243
00:16:44,336 --> 00:16:48,674
Now he switches gears
and he says, it's time for a cease fire.

244
00:16:50,175 --> 00:16:52,711
Cease fire comes on April 8th.

245
00:16:52,711 --> 00:16:55,414
Then there are actually negotiations.

246
00:16:55,414 --> 00:17:01,820
You remember when JD Vance went
to Islamabad to talk with the Iranians?

247
00:17:01,820 --> 00:17:05,157
This was on April 11th and April 12th

248
00:17:05,524 --> 00:17:08,160
about putting an end to the war.

249
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:10,729
Remember,
we have a cease fire started on April 8th.

250
00:17:10,729 --> 00:17:16,635
The 40 day bombing campaign has ended,
and April 11th, April 12th.

251
00:17:17,136 --> 00:17:21,707
Vice President Vance is talking
with the Iranians about ending the war.

252
00:17:21,740 --> 00:17:23,375
It doesn't work.

253
00:17:23,375 --> 00:17:25,878
The negotiations fail.

254
00:17:25,878 --> 00:17:28,914
The ceasefire basically remains in place.

255
00:17:28,914 --> 00:17:30,416
Very important to understand that.

256
00:17:30,416 --> 00:17:34,653
But what we do on April 13th,
the following day, April

257
00:17:34,653 --> 00:17:39,491
13th, is
we decide to employ a naval blockade

258
00:17:40,592 --> 00:17:42,361
between April

259
00:17:42,361 --> 00:17:45,864
13th and June 17th.

260
00:17:46,131 --> 00:17:52,438
The United States has a naval blockade
on the Strait of Hormuz,

261
00:17:52,438 --> 00:17:57,242
which is effectively
a naval blockade on Iran.

262
00:17:58,143 --> 00:18:03,182
Then, on June 17th, the United States

263
00:18:03,382 --> 00:18:08,921
signs the memorandum of understanding
that I described earlier.

264
00:18:08,954 --> 00:18:12,391
As I told you,
that was basically a surrender document.

265
00:18:12,424 --> 00:18:16,095
This is telling you, in effect,
and I'm getting a bit ahead of myself

266
00:18:16,095 --> 00:18:19,865
here, that the blockade did not work.

267
00:18:19,865 --> 00:18:24,069
So we signed on June 17th

268
00:18:24,103 --> 00:18:27,139
the memorandum of understanding
with the Iranians.

269
00:18:27,139 --> 00:18:31,310
And it looks like we're moving
to put an end to the war

270
00:18:31,977 --> 00:18:35,347
would then happens in

271
00:18:35,347 --> 00:18:39,518
early July,
is that the United States decides

272
00:18:39,518 --> 00:18:42,721
that it's going to violate
the memorandum of understanding.

273
00:18:42,855 --> 00:18:46,091
It's very important to understand
that article five of the Memorandum

274
00:18:46,091 --> 00:18:49,361
of Understanding says that

275
00:18:49,595 --> 00:18:52,631
Iran controls

276
00:18:54,199 --> 00:18:54,833
the Strait of

277
00:18:54,833 --> 00:18:58,303
Hormuz during the 60 day
negotiating period.

278
00:18:58,303 --> 00:19:01,907
And you understand that once
the memorandum of understanding is signed

279
00:19:01,940 --> 00:19:05,978
on June 17th,
we then move into the 60 day period

280
00:19:05,978 --> 00:19:09,882
where the two sides are going to negotiate
and deal with all those issues

281
00:19:09,882 --> 00:19:11,383
that are still on the table.

282
00:19:11,383 --> 00:19:13,585
And during the 60 day period.

283
00:19:13,585 --> 00:19:18,490
The memorandum of understanding
makes clear that Iran controls the Gulf,

284
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:22,094
but the United States
decides in early July

285
00:19:22,694 --> 00:19:27,099
that it's going to basically violate
the agreement, and the United States

286
00:19:27,099 --> 00:19:31,170
is going to create
with the Omanis, a channel

287
00:19:32,337 --> 00:19:36,875
through the Strait of Hormuz
that Iran doesn't control,

288
00:19:36,942 --> 00:19:39,978
that didn't affect
the United States controls.

289
00:19:40,112 --> 00:19:42,548
The Iranians say this is unacceptable.

290
00:19:42,548 --> 00:19:47,252
The Iranians start shooting at ships
that go through that channel.

291
00:19:47,252 --> 00:19:49,855
And of course,
the United States retaliates

292
00:19:49,855 --> 00:19:54,426
and then Iran retaliates,
and then the United States retaliates.

293
00:19:54,459 --> 00:19:56,895
This is the tip for tat campaign.

294
00:19:56,895 --> 00:19:58,664
So you see what's happened here?

295
00:19:58,664 --> 00:20:02,634
We had a 40 day air campaign, 40 day

296
00:20:02,668 --> 00:20:06,572
air campaign,
which was a discriminate air campaign

297
00:20:07,940 --> 00:20:08,840
that ended.

298
00:20:08,840 --> 00:20:11,677
And then we went to the blockade.

299
00:20:11,677 --> 00:20:14,780
And now we're involved in tit for tat.

300
00:20:14,813 --> 00:20:16,915
It starts on July 7th.

301
00:20:16,915 --> 00:20:19,184
That's
when the tit for tat campaign starts.

302
00:20:19,184 --> 00:20:23,188
And I would argue
it goes up to about July 31st.

303
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:26,024
So the cease fire is now over.

304
00:20:26,024 --> 00:20:28,994
Remember the cease fire was on April 8th
and you basically

305
00:20:28,994 --> 00:20:32,998
had a cease fire involving Iran
and the United States,

306
00:20:33,031 --> 00:20:37,035
Iran and Israel
and the Gulf states and Iran.

307
00:20:37,069 --> 00:20:40,138
You basically had a cease fire
from April 8th

308
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:43,575
up until July 7th,
when the tit for tat starts.

309
00:20:44,276 --> 00:20:47,145
The tit for tat basically lasts

310
00:20:47,145 --> 00:20:51,550
from July 7th up until July 31st.

311
00:20:51,583 --> 00:20:55,320
I would argue this past Friday,
the Iranians and the Americans

312
00:20:55,320 --> 00:20:59,458
are going back and forth,
not every day, but almost every day

313
00:20:59,458 --> 00:21:03,262
between July 7th and July 31st.

314
00:21:03,629 --> 00:21:06,198
And then what happens

315
00:21:07,165 --> 00:21:10,736
on the 30th and on the 31st is President

316
00:21:10,802 --> 00:21:16,742
Trump begins to talk about going back
to an indiscriminate air campaign.

317
00:21:16,775 --> 00:21:20,812
He's basically once again talking about

318
00:21:21,747 --> 00:21:25,417
driving the Iranians
back into the Stone age.

319
00:21:25,517 --> 00:21:30,589
And people this past weekend.

320
00:21:30,622 --> 00:21:34,259
This is August 1st, were August

321
00:21:34,259 --> 00:21:38,930
2nd, thinking that maybe President Trump
is going

322
00:21:38,997 --> 00:21:43,068
to launch this
indiscriminate air campaign.

323
00:21:43,068 --> 00:21:46,638
But what happens is, at the end of the day

324
00:21:46,672 --> 00:21:50,709
on August 1st,
he says, that's not going to happen.

325
00:21:51,043 --> 00:21:54,046
Let's go back to negotiations.

326
00:21:54,379 --> 00:21:54,713
Right.

327
00:21:54,713 --> 00:22:00,319
So remember, at the end of the 40 day
bombing campaign,

328
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:05,624
he had threatened to drive
a whole civilization to its death.

329
00:22:05,857 --> 00:22:08,493
Remember, that's his rhetoric back then.

330
00:22:08,493 --> 00:22:13,131
He was talking back then about driving the
Iranians back to the Stone age as well.

331
00:22:13,131 --> 00:22:15,133
And here he is again doing that.

332
00:22:15,133 --> 00:22:17,769
And in both cases, he didn't go that far.

333
00:22:17,769 --> 00:22:21,373
And in fact, what he did was the next day

334
00:22:21,873 --> 00:22:25,944
he called for a cease fire
the first time, April 8th.

335
00:22:25,944 --> 00:22:30,282
And this time he said, let's
go back to negotiations,

336
00:22:30,615 --> 00:22:33,352
which is another way of saying,
I think that he's interested

337
00:22:33,352 --> 00:22:38,357
now in another cease fire
so that he can negotiate.

338
00:22:39,291 --> 00:22:42,661
So that's my description of what happened.

339
00:22:42,794 --> 00:22:47,299
Now, what we want to do
is we want to analyze what happened,

340
00:22:47,466 --> 00:22:50,936
and we want to pay very, very careful

341
00:22:50,936 --> 00:22:56,742
attention
to why the Discriminate air campaign,

342
00:22:57,142 --> 00:23:03,115
the the blockade and the tit for tat
all failed.

343
00:23:03,148 --> 00:23:05,350
Those three strategies were all failed.

344
00:23:05,350 --> 00:23:08,553
If you all failed,
if you listen carefully to what I said,

345
00:23:08,587 --> 00:23:12,090
we went from discriminate air campaign

346
00:23:12,357 --> 00:23:15,360
to blockade to tit for tat,

347
00:23:15,460 --> 00:23:18,797
but we did not contemplate

348
00:23:19,231 --> 00:23:22,134
or move toward the land option.

349
00:23:22,134 --> 00:23:24,736
And we want to talk about why
that's the case.

350
00:23:24,736 --> 00:23:28,874
Nor did President Trump ever
go to an indiscriminate

351
00:23:28,874 --> 00:23:32,411
air campaign, although he threatened it,
as I tried to make clear.

352
00:23:32,411 --> 00:23:36,214
And we want to know why he didn't
do either of those

353
00:23:36,314 --> 00:23:39,518
two or employ
either of those two strategies.

354
00:23:39,551 --> 00:23:40,185
Okay,

355
00:23:41,186 --> 00:23:43,155
so let's go to the

356
00:23:43,155 --> 00:23:46,758
discriminate air campaign,
the 40 day campaign.

357
00:23:48,193 --> 00:23:51,096
Truth is, it just didn't work.

358
00:23:51,096 --> 00:23:53,665
There was no evidence,

359
00:23:53,665 --> 00:23:58,737
as that campaign wore
on, that the Iranians

360
00:23:58,737 --> 00:24:03,875
were going to throw up their hands
and surrender the shock and awe campaign.

361
00:24:03,909 --> 00:24:07,012
The decapitation strategy
which came at the end,

362
00:24:07,078 --> 00:24:11,783
came at the beginning didn't work,
and we continued to bomb.

363
00:24:11,883 --> 00:24:15,754
Most estimates say that the United States

364
00:24:15,787 --> 00:24:19,157
hit over 13,000 targets.

365
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:21,827
You want to think about that?
This is not the Israelis.

366
00:24:21,827 --> 00:24:26,298
We can't get a good number
for the Israelis, but the Americans alone

367
00:24:26,331 --> 00:24:30,335
hit 13,000 plus targets in that 40 day
campaign.

368
00:24:30,469 --> 00:24:33,472
This is a strategic bombing campaign.

369
00:24:33,638 --> 00:24:36,641
But the Iranians were not

370
00:24:36,641 --> 00:24:39,611
showing any signs of quitting.

371
00:24:39,611 --> 00:24:42,514
Furthermore,
the Iranians made it perfectly clear

372
00:24:42,514 --> 00:24:46,985
during that campaign that they had
the ability to retaliate and retaliate.

373
00:24:46,985 --> 00:24:52,023
They did, and they were inflicting
massive punishment on American bases

374
00:24:52,023 --> 00:24:57,095
in the region, on America's
Gulf state allies and on Israel itself.

375
00:24:57,095 --> 00:25:02,067
So the Iranians were doing quite
well for themselves in the fight.

376
00:25:02,067 --> 00:25:06,671
And all the time this is happening,
people are deeply worried

377
00:25:06,705 --> 00:25:10,642
that the war goes on and on
and on like this, that, number one,

378
00:25:10,642 --> 00:25:12,911
the United States
is going to run out of munitions

379
00:25:12,911 --> 00:25:17,916
because we only have a limited number
of offensive munitions

380
00:25:17,916 --> 00:25:21,720
and defensive munitions
to protect ourselves, our allies

381
00:25:21,720 --> 00:25:26,992
in the Israelis, against incoming
ballistic missiles from Iran.

382
00:25:27,158 --> 00:25:31,062
So the inventory of offensive

383
00:25:31,062 --> 00:25:34,499
and defensive weapons is being run down.

384
00:25:34,533 --> 00:25:37,702
The Iranians show no signs of quitting.

385
00:25:37,702 --> 00:25:39,070
And furthermore,

386
00:25:39,070 --> 00:25:43,942
they are retaliating in serious ways
to threaten the world economy.

387
00:25:44,342 --> 00:25:47,345
So what does President Trump do?

388
00:25:47,345 --> 00:25:49,381
What President Trump does.

389
00:25:49,381 --> 00:25:53,151
As we move towards
the end of the 40 day war, is

390
00:25:53,184 --> 00:25:58,623
that he threatens
to go to an indiscriminate air campaign.

391
00:25:59,257 --> 00:26:00,358
Just think about that.

392
00:26:00,358 --> 00:26:04,930
He's thinking about
going to an indiscriminate air campaign.

393
00:26:04,930 --> 00:26:09,868
He's talking about bombing
the Iranians back to the Stone age

394
00:26:10,001 --> 00:26:13,238
because the discriminated air
campaign has failed.

395
00:26:13,305 --> 00:26:16,908
And he sees this as the best alternative.

396
00:26:17,309 --> 00:26:22,781
But what happens is
he does not pursue that strategy.

397
00:26:22,814 --> 00:26:24,816
He does not.

398
00:26:24,816 --> 00:26:28,420
What he does is after threatening,

399
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:32,657
after threatening
to wipe out the Iranian civilization.

400
00:26:33,191 --> 00:26:38,897
He then the next day declares a cease
fire, a cease fire.

401
00:26:38,930 --> 00:26:41,700
He doesn't go up the escalation ladder.

402
00:26:41,700 --> 00:26:46,771
And the question you want to ask
yourself is why does it he do this?

403
00:26:46,771 --> 00:26:50,375
And the reason he doesn't do
this is because

404
00:26:50,375 --> 00:26:53,612
the United States does not have escalation
dominance.

405
00:26:53,678 --> 00:26:56,514
We've learned this in the 40 Day War.

406
00:26:56,514 --> 00:26:59,384
The fact is that if President

407
00:26:59,384 --> 00:27:03,655
Trump goes to an indiscriminate campaign,
that means he's going to hit

408
00:27:03,655 --> 00:27:06,891
bridges, he's
going to hit power plants, he's

409
00:27:06,891 --> 00:27:10,228
going to hit
desalination plants inside of Iran.

410
00:27:10,261 --> 00:27:12,464
He's going to hit their own facilities.

411
00:27:12,464 --> 00:27:15,500
Who's going to destroy their own
and gas facilities?

412
00:27:15,533 --> 00:27:18,737
The Iranians make it clear
they're going to do the same thing

413
00:27:18,770 --> 00:27:20,105
to all the Gulf states,

414
00:27:20,105 --> 00:27:24,442
and they're going to do
a lot of the same thing to Israel itself.

415
00:27:24,609 --> 00:27:28,980
And President Trump understands full
well he cannot prevent this.

416
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:32,717
He understands that as he goes up
the escalation ladder,

417
00:27:33,118 --> 00:27:35,987
the Iranians will go up the escalation
ladder with them.

418
00:27:35,987 --> 00:27:40,992
And you want to remember that
if in the event this were to happen

419
00:27:40,992 --> 00:27:46,131
and uranium were to destroy
all of those desalination

420
00:27:46,131 --> 00:27:50,402
plants in the Gulf states,
and they're all and gas infrastructure,

421
00:27:50,502 --> 00:27:54,739
this would have devastating consequences
for the international economy.

422
00:27:54,739 --> 00:27:58,510
And that's the last thing
that President Trump wants to have.

423
00:27:58,610 --> 00:28:04,582
So you see, it makes no sense
to go up the escalation ladder.

424
00:28:04,616 --> 00:28:08,186
This is why an indiscriminate air
campaign makes no sense.

425
00:28:08,186 --> 00:28:13,591
And it's why the next day,
after making those genocidal

426
00:28:13,591 --> 00:28:17,195
threats on April 7th,
he goes to a cease fire on the eighth.

427
00:28:17,429 --> 00:28:23,635
And the cease fire is followed
by negotiations, as I said in Islamabad.

428
00:28:23,668 --> 00:28:27,972
This is where Vice
President Vance meets with

429
00:28:29,140 --> 00:28:30,508
Iranian negotiators.

430
00:28:30,508 --> 00:28:32,711
That fails, and he has to do something.

431
00:28:32,711 --> 00:28:34,546
So what does he do?

432
00:28:34,546 --> 00:28:37,115
Does he go back to the air war? No.

433
00:28:37,115 --> 00:28:41,953
He sticks with the cease fire,
but he employs a blockade.

434
00:28:42,253 --> 00:28:43,655
He employs a blockade.

435
00:28:43,655 --> 00:28:47,225
And that starts on April 13th,

436
00:28:47,492 --> 00:28:52,230
and it runs until June 17th when you get
the memorandum of understanding.

437
00:28:52,230 --> 00:28:57,936
But the question you want to ask yourself
is, what good is the blockade?

438
00:28:57,969 --> 00:29:00,538
And the answer is it's basically no good.

439
00:29:00,538 --> 00:29:01,973
It doesn't work.

440
00:29:01,973 --> 00:29:05,910
Anybody who's studied
blockades understands that blockades,

441
00:29:05,910 --> 00:29:09,314
if they ever work,
take a long time to work.

442
00:29:09,347 --> 00:29:13,952
They take many, many months,
if not years, to strangle

443
00:29:13,985 --> 00:29:17,722
a country the size of Iran.

444
00:29:17,722 --> 00:29:20,959
So it's no accident
that between April 13th

445
00:29:20,959 --> 00:29:24,195
and June 17th,
that's just a little over two months.

446
00:29:24,229 --> 00:29:29,334
We've made very little progress
in causing the Iranians

447
00:29:29,334 --> 00:29:32,370
to throw up their hands and say, I quit.

448
00:29:32,971 --> 00:29:36,441
Therefore, having failed with the air war.

449
00:29:36,941 --> 00:29:41,679
And that's the discriminate air campaign
being unwilling

450
00:29:41,713 --> 00:29:46,985
to go to an indiscriminate
air campaign, having failed with

451
00:29:48,219 --> 00:29:49,788
the blockade.

452
00:29:49,788 --> 00:29:54,058
On June 17th, President Trump signs
the memorandum of understanding.

453
00:29:54,058 --> 00:29:58,596
And as I made clear at the top of the
show, that's a surrender document, okay.

454
00:29:58,630 --> 00:30:03,935
And President Trump signs that agreement.

455
00:30:04,102 --> 00:30:07,372
He can't bring himself to stick to it.

456
00:30:07,438 --> 00:30:12,377
The thought of the United States losing,
the thought of Donald Trump

457
00:30:12,577 --> 00:30:16,381
losing a war that he started to

458
00:30:16,381 --> 00:30:19,384
Iran is just unacceptable.

459
00:30:19,384 --> 00:30:24,322
So he begins he begins to challenge,

460
00:30:24,322 --> 00:30:27,392
to undermine
the memorandum of understanding.

461
00:30:27,392 --> 00:30:32,063
He begins to look for ways
to put pressure on the Iranians

462
00:30:32,096 --> 00:30:35,099
again, to get the Iranians
to throw their hands up.

463
00:30:35,400 --> 00:30:40,438
And this is the start of the tit
for tat campaign, right.

464
00:30:40,471 --> 00:30:45,476
As I said to you,
as soon as the Americans

465
00:30:46,211 --> 00:30:50,748
establish this channel
in the Strait of Hormuz, contrary

466
00:30:50,748 --> 00:30:54,152
to what's in article
five of the memorandum of understanding,

467
00:30:54,385 --> 00:30:59,090
the Iranians start shooting at ships
that are going through that channel.

468
00:30:59,090 --> 00:31:02,560
We retaliate with air attacks,

469
00:31:02,560 --> 00:31:05,663
and the Iranians
then retaliate against us.

470
00:31:05,663 --> 00:31:07,265
And of course, we retaliate.

471
00:31:07,265 --> 00:31:10,435
They retaliate,
and we're going up the escalation ladder.

472
00:31:10,435 --> 00:31:12,170
But it's just tit for tat.

473
00:31:12,170 --> 00:31:16,441
And what you want to understand here
is that a tit for tat air

474
00:31:16,474 --> 00:31:22,113
strategy is much less ambitious than that

475
00:31:22,113 --> 00:31:25,583
strategic bombing campaign that we waged

476
00:31:26,017 --> 00:31:28,786
during the first 40 days of the conflict.

477
00:31:28,786 --> 00:31:32,790
And you just say to yourself,
if that strategic bombing campaign,

478
00:31:32,790 --> 00:31:37,862
even though it was a discriminating
bombing campaign, when it discriminated

479
00:31:37,862 --> 00:31:41,532
in terms of the targets,
it was still a substantial bombing

480
00:31:41,532 --> 00:31:45,770
campaign, 13,000
plus targets by the United States alone.

481
00:31:46,738 --> 00:31:50,675
If that right couldn't

482
00:31:50,675 --> 00:31:54,345
bring the Iranians to their knees,
why would anybody think that

483
00:31:54,345 --> 00:31:58,116
a tit for tat strategy is going to bring
the Iranians to their knees?

484
00:31:58,116 --> 00:31:59,651
And in fact, it didn't.

485
00:31:59,651 --> 00:32:03,955
And in fact, the tit for tat strategy
was causing the United States.

486
00:32:03,988 --> 00:32:07,759
You'd probably in fact,
we were beginning to move

487
00:32:07,792 --> 00:32:13,731
our military assets out of the Persian
Gulf, back to Jordan and back to Israel.

488
00:32:13,731 --> 00:32:15,733
And what did the Iranians do?

489
00:32:15,733 --> 00:32:20,104
They started targeting Jordan,
and they were doing substantial damage

490
00:32:20,104 --> 00:32:25,176
to American military assets in Jordan,
which is outside the Persian Gulf.

491
00:32:25,310 --> 00:32:29,280
All of this just shows you
that escalation, dominance,

492
00:32:29,314 --> 00:32:32,383
whether you're talking about the

493
00:32:33,384 --> 00:32:34,919
the Discriminant

494
00:32:34,919 --> 00:32:39,424
Air campaign or the indiscriminate
air campaign, or you're talking about

495
00:32:39,457 --> 00:32:42,760
tit for tat,
you go up the escalation ladder

496
00:32:42,760 --> 00:32:45,797
in either of those three cases,

497
00:32:45,830 --> 00:32:49,100
and it's not clear that America wins.

498
00:32:49,100 --> 00:32:52,603
And in fact, it's clear to me
that Iran wins.

499
00:32:52,637 --> 00:32:56,441
So the end result is that

500
00:32:56,441 --> 00:32:59,477
President Trump laid on Saturday.

501
00:32:59,510 --> 00:33:05,416
This is August 1st,
I believe it was August 2nd in Iran, said,

502
00:33:05,416 --> 00:33:11,689
I'm not going to try to bomb Iran
back to the Stone age.

503
00:33:11,756 --> 00:33:16,594
And what we now have to do
is we have to go back to negotiations.

504
00:33:17,061 --> 00:33:20,331
Now, keep in mind here

505
00:33:20,398 --> 00:33:24,602
that there were two strategies
that we never employed.

506
00:33:24,802 --> 00:33:29,073
We never employed the indiscriminate air
campaign, number one.

507
00:33:29,073 --> 00:33:32,076
And I explained why that was the case.

508
00:33:32,410 --> 00:33:35,913
We do not have escalation dominance

509
00:33:35,913 --> 00:33:40,051
as you go up the escalation ladder
to that level.

510
00:33:40,318 --> 00:33:40,852
Right.

511
00:33:40,852 --> 00:33:44,655
And then we did not
pursue a land campaign.

512
00:33:44,655 --> 00:33:47,091
And let me say a few words about that.

513
00:33:48,893 --> 00:33:50,561
To actually

514
00:33:50,561 --> 00:33:53,998
conquer the Strait of Hormuz,

515
00:33:54,499 --> 00:33:57,402
I believe, would involve more

516
00:33:57,402 --> 00:34:02,140
than 100,000 troops,
would involve a huge fighting force,

517
00:34:02,507 --> 00:34:06,978
and many Americans
would die in the process.

518
00:34:07,211 --> 00:34:11,549
There is no way that President Trump
is willing to do that.

519
00:34:11,549 --> 00:34:15,153
In fact, there's no way
the American people would tolerate that,

520
00:34:15,186 --> 00:34:15,753
which, of course,

521
00:34:15,753 --> 00:34:19,424
is one of the reasons that President Trump
never went down that road.

522
00:34:19,557 --> 00:34:24,429
We would need, in other words,
a good 100,000 combat troops,

523
00:34:24,462 --> 00:34:29,067
maybe 150,000 combat troops
in the Persian Gulf

524
00:34:29,333 --> 00:34:33,471
to conquer enough territory
to control the Strait of Hormuz.

525
00:34:33,538 --> 00:34:36,974
And if you were talking about conquering
all of Iran

526
00:34:37,041 --> 00:34:40,111
the way we conquered all of Ukraine,
excuse me, the way we conquered

527
00:34:40,111 --> 00:34:45,016
all of Iraq in 2003, you're talking
about hundreds of thousands of troops.

528
00:34:45,016 --> 00:34:46,417
That was not going to happen.

529
00:34:46,417 --> 00:34:50,321
We were not going to try to conquer.

530
00:34:51,522 --> 00:34:53,424
All of you, all of Iran.

531
00:34:53,424 --> 00:34:54,659
We were not even going to try

532
00:34:54,659 --> 00:34:58,396
to conquer enough territory
to control the Strait of Hormuz.

533
00:34:58,429 --> 00:35:02,934
So what people ended up doing
was talking about conquering an island

534
00:35:02,934 --> 00:35:06,704
or two in the Persian Gulf
that belonged to Iran,

535
00:35:06,737 --> 00:35:10,508
but President Trump
was not even willing to do that.

536
00:35:10,575 --> 00:35:16,314
And if you look at the number of combat
troops that we had in the Persian

537
00:35:16,314 --> 00:35:17,748
Gulf, it's quite clear

538
00:35:17,748 --> 00:35:21,319
that we were never serious
about even trying the land option.

539
00:35:21,352 --> 00:35:26,157
I would estimate that at the most,
we had 8000 combat troops,

540
00:35:26,190 --> 00:35:31,229
8000 troops that you could use for land
attack in the Persian Gulf

541
00:35:31,262 --> 00:35:36,300
at any point
since February 28th, and 8000 troops

542
00:35:36,400 --> 00:35:40,938
trying to conquer even an island
in the Persian Gulf against the Iranians

543
00:35:41,005 --> 00:35:46,277
in the heat of the summer
would be an almost impossible task.

544
00:35:46,277 --> 00:35:49,080
But furthermore,
what if we did conquer an island?

545
00:35:49,080 --> 00:35:51,682
What would be the result?

546
00:35:51,682 --> 00:35:56,654
What's the story that one might tell about
how conquering an island

547
00:35:56,954 --> 00:35:59,891
puts an end to this war?

548
00:35:59,891 --> 00:36:05,129
Has conquering an island
get the Iranians to throw their hands up?

549
00:36:05,196 --> 00:36:06,931
The answer is it doesn't.

550
00:36:06,931 --> 00:36:08,833
We have no land option here.

551
00:36:08,833 --> 00:36:10,201
We don't have the troops.

552
00:36:10,201 --> 00:36:14,105
We don't have the
stomach for a land war and

553
00:36:15,373 --> 00:36:17,441
a minor attack

554
00:36:17,441 --> 00:36:21,946
on an island
or landing somewhere on the coast of Iran

555
00:36:21,979 --> 00:36:26,784
has little effect
on the outcome of the war.

556
00:36:26,817 --> 00:36:29,453
So there's no land. Option number one.

557
00:36:29,453 --> 00:36:32,456
Number two, there is no

558
00:36:34,025 --> 00:36:37,028
indiscriminate air option.

559
00:36:37,562 --> 00:36:40,097
Strategic bombing
of an indiscriminate sort

560
00:36:40,097 --> 00:36:44,035
going against the entire target
set inside of Iran.

561
00:36:44,068 --> 00:36:45,336
That doesn't work either.

562
00:36:45,336 --> 00:36:48,973
So you're left with three strategies
a discriminatory campaign,

563
00:36:48,973 --> 00:36:51,976
which we tried and failed.

564
00:36:53,177 --> 00:36:55,813
A blockade, which we tried and failed.

565
00:36:55,813 --> 00:36:59,917
Tic-Tac tit for tat,
which we tried and failed.

566
00:37:01,219 --> 00:37:02,620
And here we are.

567
00:37:02,620 --> 00:37:06,857
So the question is,
what do we do moving forward?

568
00:37:07,625 --> 00:37:11,062
Well, it seems manifestly clear to me

569
00:37:11,429 --> 00:37:16,701
that we've tried
all the strategies that are available

570
00:37:17,001 --> 00:37:19,904
and they have not worked on,

571
00:37:19,904 --> 00:37:24,675
surprisingly, and the two strategies
that we have not tried

572
00:37:24,675 --> 00:37:30,548
or not a solution to the problem
and to go back to the goals

573
00:37:30,815 --> 00:37:36,420
we have failed to achieve any of our goals
up to this point.

574
00:37:36,787 --> 00:37:41,859
It's manifestly clear when you look
at the memorandum of understanding

575
00:37:41,892 --> 00:37:46,697
signed on June 17th,
and when you just think about where we are

576
00:37:46,697 --> 00:37:51,636
today in terms of those goals
and in terms of who controls the stray

577
00:37:51,936 --> 00:37:54,071
and what's happened to our basing

578
00:37:54,071 --> 00:37:56,674
structure, what's happened
to our alliance structure in the Gulf?

579
00:37:56,674 --> 00:37:59,176
It's clear that we've lost.

580
00:37:59,176 --> 00:38:02,346
We have failed
to achieve our goals and worse.

581
00:38:02,346 --> 00:38:08,519
And this is reflected in the June 17th
memorandum of understanding.

582
00:38:08,519 --> 00:38:09,320
As I said to you,

583
00:38:09,320 --> 00:38:13,958
if you look carefully at that memorandum,
it's a surrender document.

584
00:38:14,358 --> 00:38:17,161
So what is President Trump
going to do now?

585
00:38:17,161 --> 00:38:19,263
Now, I would point out
that when it comes to President

586
00:38:19,263 --> 00:38:22,933
Trump, you can never be absolutely certain
what he will do.

587
00:38:22,933 --> 00:38:27,104
And in a situation where he's desperate
and he is desperate

588
00:38:27,104 --> 00:38:30,541
because he is surely sophisticated
enough to know

589
00:38:30,775 --> 00:38:36,147
that he is in deep trouble in this war
and that he is, in effect, lost the war.

590
00:38:36,147 --> 00:38:40,451
So he may lash out
and he may do something foolish.

591
00:38:40,451 --> 00:38:46,390
But assuming that's not the case,
he really has no choice at this point,

592
00:38:46,390 --> 00:38:50,828
but to pursue
another memorandum of understanding

593
00:38:51,362 --> 00:38:54,098
to try to get a deal

594
00:38:54,098 --> 00:38:57,868
with the Iranians as quickly as possible.

595
00:38:58,269 --> 00:39:00,771
I want to point out two things here.

596
00:39:00,771 --> 00:39:05,376
One is, President
Trump would have been much better off

597
00:39:05,976 --> 00:39:11,549
cutting a deal immediately
after the April 8th ceasefire,

598
00:39:11,549 --> 00:39:17,355
when the bombing campaign failed
to discriminate, air campaign failed.

599
00:39:18,689 --> 00:39:20,958
On April 8th, he moved to a cease fire.

600
00:39:20,958 --> 00:39:24,095
He should have then tried to cut a deal.

601
00:39:24,628 --> 00:39:27,998
Furthermore, when the blockade failed

602
00:39:27,998 --> 00:39:32,136
and he signed a memorandum
of understanding on June 17th,

603
00:39:32,570 --> 00:39:36,507
he should have stuck to that
memorandum of understanding,

604
00:39:36,507 --> 00:39:39,543
and he should have gone to great lengths
to work out

605
00:39:39,543 --> 00:39:42,947
a deal with Iran to put an end to the war.

606
00:39:42,947 --> 00:39:45,015
But as I told you, he didn't do that.

607
00:39:45,015 --> 00:39:50,554
Instead, he tried to violate article
five of the memorandum of understanding

608
00:39:50,554 --> 00:39:54,759
we got in this tit for tat strategy
for almost the entire month of July.

609
00:39:54,825 --> 00:39:55,826
It failed.

610
00:39:55,826 --> 00:40:00,097
And now I'm telling you, it's
time to cut a deal.

611
00:40:00,131 --> 00:40:05,569
Although I'm arguing that it would have
been smarter to cut the deal earlier.

612
00:40:05,569 --> 00:40:10,508
One final point on this
is that it's going to be tougher

613
00:40:10,508 --> 00:40:13,511
to get a memorandum of understanding

614
00:40:13,577 --> 00:40:17,515
from the Iranians moving forward.

615
00:40:17,815 --> 00:40:21,952
That is as good as the memorandum of

616
00:40:21,952 --> 00:40:26,257
understanding
that the president signed on June 17th.

617
00:40:27,024 --> 00:40:31,462
The Iranians are more aware than ever
that they're in the driver's seat.

618
00:40:31,495 --> 00:40:36,133
There are more aware than ever
that President Trump is in deep trouble

619
00:40:36,600 --> 00:40:39,670
and that he needs an agreement.

620
00:40:39,670 --> 00:40:44,108
So they're going to drive a hard bargain
or a harder bargain

621
00:40:44,108 --> 00:40:48,712
for sure, than they drove in the run
up to the June 17th memorandum.

622
00:40:48,712 --> 00:40:52,917
And a harder bargain,
I believe, than they would have driven

623
00:40:52,917 --> 00:40:57,822
back in April after a cease
fire was declared on the eighth.

624
00:40:57,822 --> 00:41:02,359
So there's no question
that President Trump and the United States

625
00:41:02,660 --> 00:41:07,298
is in really deep trouble here,
and getting a peace

626
00:41:07,298 --> 00:41:13,170
agreement is going to be 
not an easy task.

627
00:41:13,170 --> 00:41:17,575
But the bottom line,
and this is where I'll stop,

628
00:41:17,575 --> 00:41:21,679
is that President Trump has no choice.

629
00:41:21,912 --> 00:41:27,952
He has no military strategy
that he can employ

630
00:41:28,219 --> 00:41:34,158
to reverse the dire situation
that he finds himself in.

631
00:41:34,592 --> 00:41:38,863
The fact is, he foolishly started a war

632
00:41:39,497 --> 00:41:44,602
on February 28th
that he was destined to lose.

633
00:41:44,602 --> 00:41:47,872
Many of his advisers understood full well

634
00:41:48,239 --> 00:41:53,677
that the strategy that he was employing,
this is the discriminatory campaign

635
00:41:53,677 --> 00:41:58,082
that I described earlier,
was destined to fail and fail it did,

636
00:41:58,082 --> 00:42:01,785
and there was no viable
alternative strategy.

637
00:42:01,785 --> 00:42:06,757
And there still is no viable
alternative strategy.

638
00:42:06,757 --> 00:42:09,827
So it's time to cut a deal.

639
00:42:09,827 --> 00:42:14,598
But that is not going
to be easy for him to do. So

640
00:42:15,666 --> 00:42:16,467
let's just

641
00:42:16,467 --> 00:42:20,471
hope that things work out,
that in the month or months ahead,

642
00:42:20,471 --> 00:42:24,074
he's able to put an end to this war once
and for all.

643
00:42:24,475 --> 00:42:30,314
Thank you very much for listening to my
video and I look forward to the next one.

